Z||000009||1FST2M6||09-10-2001||01:54 PM||||well i destroyed the drivers side wheel bearing, and broke 2 of the left wheel studs. i'll get a pic... it was making HIDEOUS noises sat-sun and this morning.. i just figured it was rubbing the disc on the splash sheild... well on my way to lunch just a bit ago it started to shake REALLLY bad. i pulled over in a parking lot and there was grease all over the wheel.. i pulled the cover off the wheel and 2 of the studs are snapped off and the nuts rattleing around behind the cover. SOOOO... my car is going to the shop tonite.. i've already got 20 new wheel studs, and both rear bearing assemblies on their way from NAPA... should be back on the road tomorrow night...    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">  oh well i'd rather break that than spin a rod bearing. <P>I'm wondering how long it'll last too.. if i get 10 bottles out of it i'll be suprised. (about 60 shots) i refilled it friday, again later saturday.. and i've got 3lbs left.  <P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/1fstsun21.jpg"> <p>[This message has been edited by 1FST2M6 (edited 09-10-2001).]||||reg||1
