Z||000015||1FST2M6||09-10-2001||04:56 PM||||nitrous and fuel jets are in hundredths of an inch. .052 .041 .038 well reall from .005 to .60 (1000hp shot on a methanol funny car)<P><BR>.052 of  1 inch. the jets are about the size of a pencil eraser. but the holes vary. the biiger the # the more either fuel or nitrous.  the trick is to find the best balance of the 2 and not to destroy the engine in the mean time. paying attention ot the air / fuel ratio and injector duty cycle so your not straining anything to much. <BR>||||reg||1
